Chosen R=50 m, K=8: miss rate 0.85%, 5.47 candidates per point.
R=20, K=8 is smaller (3.63 per point) but misses 1.82%.
R=100, K=12 misses 0.57% but needs 8.89 per point (1.6x more rows for the classifier and HMM).
Above R=50 the miss rate does not change: a point only gets a label if it is within 50 m of its arc (labels.MAX_LABEL_DIST), so beyond 50 m only K matters. Remaining misses at R=50 come from the K cap.
K=12 at R=50 cuts misses to 0.57% for 1.23x the rows - a possible v2 change if the classifier handles larger sets well.
